## What Problem This Solves

Fixes an issue where a configured Comfy `workflowPath` could make OpenClaw read an arbitrarily large local JSON file into memory before parsing or failing.

## Why This Change Was Made

Comfy now supports an opt-in `workflowFileMaxBytes` read boundary on the shared `workflowPath` loader. For workflow paths configured under `plugins.entries.comfy.config`, leaving the setting unset preserves the existing uncapped read behavior; setting it makes files above the limit fail locally with actionable guidance before any provider request.

The reader stays in the shared Comfy workflow owner, so image, video, and music workflows use the same behavior. Inline workflow objects are unchanged.

Comfy workflow settings—including `workflow`, `workflowPath`, `promptNodeId`, and the `image`, `video`, and `music` sections—belong under `plugins.entries.comfy.config`. The strict core `models.providers.comfy` schema still accepts provider-level connection and authentication fields such as `baseUrl`, `apiKey`, `auth`, and `headers`, but rejects Comfy workflow keys.

## User Impact

Uncapped workflow reads remain the default for supported plugin-root configuration, and operators can opt into a documented file-size boundary that matches ComfyUI's default `--max-upload-size`.

## Evidence

- Rebased exact-head real call-chain proof (`c03cbf17a34abce620ff9e901b7dad5ccce36da8`, validation base `ff136c3cc5cde2e150e5f9324f59260b00380e45`): a localhost HTTP fixture replaces only the external Comfy service while the production `buildComfyImageGenerationProvider` loads a symlinked workflow through both the default uncapped and configured capped paths, submits it, polls history, and downloads an image. Proof source SHA256: `78754084b09347254bc0c9da88a46f00d2612df4002e62341b1ac138ff9565c6`.
- Rebased exact-head large-file proof: the same production call chain accepts a parseable 16,777,338-byte workflow under the explicit 100 MiB cap; a 100 MiB+1 sparse workflow is rejected with actionable guidance before the fixture receives another HTTP request.
- Symlink behavior is visible at the production boundary: both default and configured provider paths follow the symlink while leaving the link intact. FIFO rejection is tested through provider generation; it must fail before any Comfy HTTP request, with the writer process terminated and awaited and no wall-clock timeout race.
- Config validation covers the canonical plugin-root workflow settings; core `models.providers.comfy` accepts provider-level connection/authentication fields and rejects Comfy workflow keys.
- Focused Vitest suites: 89 passed across four files in the local worktree. Docker isolation could not start because this host has no Docker daemon.

