## What Problem This Solves

Keeps a later LINE batch rejection from dropping valid reply parts after an earlier batch was accepted.

Fixes #142734

## Why This Change Was Made

Mixed LINE reply parts stay ordered and use batches of up to five. When a later batch gets definitive HTTP 400, remaining parts receive single-message retries before accepted receipts are combined; failures remain visible in the partial receipt. Recovery deduplicates receipt IDs already recorded for accepted sends, including cumulative receipts from a throwing delivery observer.

## User Impact

Mixed replies use fewer provider requests; a rejected later batch no longer drops valid text, and callers receive every accepted message ID without replaying an accepted batch.

## Evidence

- At pinned validation base `fd80f72fa0cba77784b759cc9533048fb48a9b4d` and exact HEAD `36caafd7a09d45c34d446b7ca4c4aa0d7af5bd9e`, the production-path harness sends Flex, location, and text in 3 ordered POSTs at base and 1 POST at HEAD; unchanged plain text uses 1 POST at both revisions.
- Later-batch fault at exact HEAD: the first five-message POST returns 200; the later text+image POST returns 400; text retry returns 200 and image retry returns 400. The partial receipt contains six accepted IDs (the first five plus recovered text), with no replay of the first batch.
- Observer-failure fault at exact HEAD: after a mixed Flex+text batch returns 400, Flex retry returns 200 and its delivery observer throws; text retry still returns 200. Final `receipt.parts` and `messageIds` each contain exactly the two accepted IDs. At the pinned base, the observer stops the unbatched send after the first accepted Flex.
- Unit regressions verify observer failure does not turn `[A, B]` into `[A, B, A]`, and ordinary partial recovery preserves `[A, B, C]` once each.
- Exact-head controls: invalid media preparation preserves accepted Flex and text IDs; malformed HTTP 200 receipt recovery preserves accepted IDs; media-only and plain-text sends each use 1 POST.
- Focused LINE send and batch suites passed: 38/38 tests. The loopback harness redirects only LINE API push requests; it makes no request to LINE or the supplied media URL.
- Contract: [LINE Messaging API: Sending messages](https://developers.line.biz/en/docs/messaging-api/sending-messages/) accepts up to five message objects per request.

