### Impact

Affected users: none visible today. Anyone who reads `acp_messages.created_at` or `acp_tool_calls.created_at` later (a per-message time in an ACP client, audit, forensics by SQL as in #10788, a retention policy) sees rows of a trimmed session stamped with the time of the last trim. The draft PR #11622 would read these columns and show them in the ZeroCode transcript; if it merges, sessions that went through a trim on `zeroclaw acp` or the gateway WebSocket ACP would show the trim time on every message.
Frequency: at every trim of a session served by `zeroclaw acp` or the gateway WebSocket ACP (live history trimmed during a turn, or a restore that trims). Sessions served only through the ZeroCode/daemon RPC path are not affected by this writer.
Consequence: the per-message time is lost for good in storage; fixing the writer later does not bring the overwritten values back.

